@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2507 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1301 x i8] }> <{ [1301 x i8] c"# `doc_cfg`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#43781]\0A\0A------\0A\0AThe `doc_cfg` feature allows an API be documented as only available in some specific platforms.\0AThis attribute has two effects:\0A\0A1. In the annotated item's documentation, there will be a message saying \22Available on\0A    (platform) only\22.\0A\0A2. The item's doc-tests will only run on the specific platform.\0A\0AIn addition to allowing the use of the `#[doc(cfg)]` attribute, this feature enables the use of a\0Aspecial conditional compilation flag, `#[cfg(doc)]`, set whenever building documentation on your\0Acrate.\0A\0AThis feature was introduced as part of PR [#43348] to allow the platform-specific parts of the\0Astandard library be documented.\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(doc_cfg)]\0A\0A#[cfg(any(windows, doc))]\0A#[doc(cfg(windows))]\0A/// The application's icon in the notification area (a.k.a. system tray).\0A///\0A/// # Examples\0A///\0A/// ```no_run\0A/// extern crate my_awesome_ui_library;\0A/// use my_awesome_ui_library::current_app;\0A/// use my_awesome_ui_library::windows::notification;\0A///\0A/// let icon = current_app().get::<notification::Icon>();\0A/// icon.show();\0A/// icon.show_message(\22Hello\22);\0A/// ```\0Apub struct Icon {\0A    // ...\0A}\0A```\0A\0A[#43781]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/43781\0A[#43348]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/43348\0A" }>, align 1
@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2508 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [12 x i8] }> <{ [12 x i8] c"doc_cfg_hide" }>, align 1
