@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2510 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [10 x i8] }> <{ [10 x i8] c"doc_masked" }>, align 1
@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2511 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1021 x i8] }> <{ [1021 x i8] c"# `doc_masked`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#44027]\0A\0A-----\0A\0AThe `doc_masked` feature allows a crate to exclude types from a given crate from appearing in lists\0Aof trait implementations. The specifics of the feature are as follows:\0A\0A1. When rustdoc encounters an `extern crate` statement annotated with a `#[doc(masked)]` attribute,\0A   it marks the crate as being masked.\0A\0A2. When listing traits a given type implements, rustdoc ensures that traits from masked crates are\0A   not emitted into the documentation.\0A\0A3. When listing types that implement a given trait, rustdoc ensures that types from masked crates\0A   are not emitted into the documentation.\0A\0AThis feature was introduced in PR [#44026] to ensure that compiler-internal and\0Aimplementation-specific types and traits were not included in the standard library's documentation.\0ASuch types would introduce broken links into the documentation.\0A\0A[#44026]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/44026\0A[#44027]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/44027\0A" }>, align 1
@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2512 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [17 x i8] }> <{ [17 x i8] c"doc_notable_trait" }>, align 1
@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.2513 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1106 x i8] }> <{ [1106 x i8] c"# `doc_notable_trait`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#45040]\0A\0AThe `doc_notable_trait` feature allows the use of the `#[doc(notable_trait)]`\0Aattribute, which will display the trait in a \22Notable traits\22 dialog for\0Afunctions returning types that implement the trait. For example, this attribute\0Ais applied to the `Iterator`, `Future`, `io::Read`, and `io::Write` traits in\0Athe standard library.\0A\0AYou can do this on your own traits like so:\0A\0A```\0A#![feature(doc_notable_trait)]\0A\0A#[doc(notable_trait)]\0Apub trait MyTrait {}\0A\0Apub struct MyStruct;\0Aimpl MyTrait for MyStruct {}\0A\0A/// The docs for this function will have a button that displays a dialog about\0A/// `MyStruct` implementing `MyTrait`.\0Apub fn my_fn() -> MyStruct { MyStruct }\0A```\0A\0AThis feature was originally implemented in PR [#45039].\0A\0ASee also its documentation in [the rustdoc book][rustdoc-book-notable_trait].\0A\0A[#45040]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/45040\0A[#45039]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/45039\0A[rustdoc-book-notable_trait]: ../../rustdoc/unstable-features.html#adding-your-trait-to-the-notable-traits-dialog\0A" }>, align 1
