@anon.3c5d4856225436a016f648d8ca8332b3.3008 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1175 x i8] }> <{ [1175 x i8] c"# `rustc_attrs`\0A\0AThis feature has no tracking issue, and is therefore internal to\0Athe compiler, not being intended for general use.\0A\0ANote: `rustc_attrs` enables many rustc-internal attributes and this page\0Aonly discuss a few of them.\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AThe `rustc_attrs` feature allows debugging rustc type layouts by using\0A`#[rustc_layout(...)]` to debug layout at compile time (it even works\0Awith `cargo check`) as an alternative to `rustc -Z print-type-sizes`\0Athat is way more verbose.\0A\0AOptions provided by `#[rustc_layout(...)]` are `debug`, `size`, `align`,\0A`abi`. Note that it only works on sized types without generics.\0A\0A## Examples\0A\0A```rust,compile_fail\0A#![feature(rustc_attrs)]\0A\0A#[rustc_layout(abi, size)]\0Apub enum X {\0A    Y(u8, u8, u8),\0A    Z(isize),\0A}\0A```\0A\0AWhen that is compiled, the compiler will error with something like\0A\0A```text\0Aerror: abi: Aggregate { sized: true }\0A --> src/lib.rs:4:1\0A  |\0A4 | / pub enum T {\0A5 | |     Y(u8, u8, u8),\0A6 | |     Z(isize),\0A7 | | }\0A  | |_^\0A\0Aerror: size: Size { raw: 16 }\0A --> src/lib.rs:4:1\0A  |\0A4 | / pub enum T {\0A5 | |     Y(u8, u8, u8),\0A6 | |     Z(isize),\0A7 | | }\0A  | |_^\0A\0Aerror: aborting due to 2 previous errors\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
